[h2]3D Icons[/h2]
Draws in-world symbols in side colors above infantry, vehicles and operated drones of your side, up to your view distance. Members of your own group also get a marker that shows whether they are alive, unconscious or dead. Icons shrink with distance. Names and some labels disappear as the icon gets smaller; hold either Windows key to show all of them.

The server can choose which sides are visible in play and while spectating, whether to draw units in spectator mode, whether to show names, and whether to hide units behind objects. Group member markers have separate settings for hiding them behind cover and for applying the view distance limit. Players can hide the overlay in the Client tab.

[h2]How to enable it[/h2]
In Eden, place the [b]3D Icons[/b] module to use it in that scenario. Enable it without an Eden module through [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=450814997]CBA_A3[/url]. Open [b]Addon Options → 3D Icons[/b], check [b]Enable 3D Icons[/b] and restart the mission. In multiplayer, use the Server tab.

